{
  "_notes": {
    "license": "All assets CC0 1.0. See CREDITS.md.",
    "sunAzimuthDeg": "Measured from the brightest region of each 1k HDR: azimuth = u*360 where u is the horizontal equirect coordinate (0..1, left edge = 0). sunDir is the matching unit vector in three.js world space for an un-rotated scene.environment/background (three.js equirect: u = atan2(z,x)/2pi + 0.5). If you rotate the env (backgroundRotation/environmentRotation), rotate sunDir the same way.",
    "tex": "All 1k JPG. nor = OpenGL normal (+Y). arm = glTF-style packed AO (R) / Roughness (G) / Metalness (B): use it as aoMap + roughnessMap + metalnessMap in three.js. rough = greyscale roughness. metres = real-world width one tile covers (ambientCG sizes approximate).",
    "models": "Meshopt + WebP compressed: three.js GLTFLoader needs setMeshoptDecoder(MeshoptDecoder) from three/examples/jsm/libs/meshopt_decoder.module.js. sizeM = real-world bounding box [w,h,d] in metres at scale 1 (origin at base). Several props are small in real life (rock 7cm, basket, plant) - scale them up in-game.",
    "hdri2k": "2k .hdr versions were NOT downloaded (would add ~31 MB and break the 40 MB budget). 2k sizes are in each entry (size2kMB); URL pattern https://dl.polyhaven.org/file/ph-assets/HDRIs/hdr/2k/<id>_2k.hdr"
  },
